    "raw_gdf15": "raw GDF15 is not in this table and cannot be. It is published in sheet GDF15-1 as six anonymous cohort columns of unequal length, with no patient identifier, no age and no row order shared with the per-patient sheets, so there is no key to attach it to a clinical row and none can be constructed without guessing which patient goes with which value",
    "note": "the patients complete on all five clinical measurements are a small and strongly case-enriched subset: PVOD is 43.5% of them against 15.7% of the full cohort, about three times enriched. This is not a smaller version of the study but a different group of patients, because whether a patient has a measurement depends on their diagnosis and depends on it most for the variables missing most often. A complete-case comparison therefore cannot confirm the full-cohort comparator ranking, and the rankings among the clinical variables do move substantially at this sample size. These rows are not an unbiased re-estimate of any AUC: they are conditional on the measurement being available, and availability is associated with diagnosis"
  },
